title: "Homelessness SBA — Part 2: Integrating Disciplinary Insights"
authors: 'Omer Ari, Ben Pierce, Lia Haddadian, and Piotr Mitros'
description: 'Part 2 of a three-part interdisciplinary-reasoning SBA. The Comm360 intern team (Ty, Peggy, Lacy, with supervisor Lianne Park) integrates the six disciplinary insights from Part 1: they build a concept map whose arrows show how strongly the evidence supports each connection, interpret an exhibit film that uses a ship as a metaphor for housing instability, revise the film to represent structural inequality, and write a poem that communicates the relationships the map revealed.'
~~~~

Welcome to Part 2 [id=hs2_welcome_sec]
--------------------------------------

Instructor: Welcome to Part 2 Module of the **Interdisciplinary Research Process (IRP) Scenario-based Activity**.

  Part 2 should take around 1 to 2 hours, and you can break it up over several days if you'd like. It is due November 22, 2026.

  In this module, you’ll apply what you know about interdisciplinary research process. The module contains everything you need to complete the project.

  There are instructions on the screen to help you navigate and give your answers. There are also a few links embedded in the text. You can use them for additional information, but that’s optional.

  Remember that I will be seeing these results, so please take it seriously and do your best work. I think you'll enjoy it.

  Click the Continue button to start.

Reviewing Our Sources [id=hs2_review]
-------------------------------------

Lianne: If you recall, in Part 1, we brainstormed and learned about causes of housing insecurity. That helped us understand this is a complex problem with multiple parts, which makes it suitable for interdisciplinary study. We then located sources from different disciplines shedding light and insight on those causes.

  In this part, we will see how the disciplinary insights can be integrated for a more comprehensive understanding of this problem. But first let’s review the sources we consulted.

::hs2_recall_screen [display=target:hs2_main label="What do you remember?"]

Lianne: Before we begin integrating the disciplinary perspectives, let’s see what you remember from Part 1. On the right is the comparison table we built as we reviewed the six studies, but a few pieces are missing.

  **Fill in the missing cells as best you can from memory. You don’t need to remember the exact wording—just capture the main idea.**

