Peggy: I think this relationship may work in both directions. Limited access to support programs may worsen stress and housing instability, while severe mental health challenges may also increase the need for coordinated housing and support services. Since the relationship seems conceptually strong but was not directly examined across the studies, a double dashed arrow may work best here.

::hs2_map14 [display=target:hs2_main label="Our completed concept map"]

